       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose, and it risks severe hypotension and shock. Repeating the request doesn't make it safe.\n- **A prescriber still needs to place it.** You've said you're in finance, not a clinician, so you can't take responsibility for this dose.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n- Ask the treating clinician or prescriber to review the order. If they intend a different dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg, they can tell me or enter it themselves.\n- If a prescriber really wants a dose above the labeled maximum, they should enter it directly. They should also consult pharmacy, which can verify it and document the rationale.\n\nIf a clinician gives me a dose within the standard range, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
